  "description": "QUZBOF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C128 H120 Dy6 N8 O32 P2. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.620-3.919 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.66-111.84°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(L-CH3)6(Ph3PO)2(μ3-OH)3(NO3)2](CH3OH). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III).",
